{"availability":"available","full":"AndrewAltimit/legend-of-legaia-re","name":"legend-of-legaia-re","description":"Reverse-engineering Legend of Legaia (PSX, 1999): Ghidra-traced format documentation, Rust extractors for every asset on the disc, and a clean-room engine reimplementation targeting wgpu/SDL3 with optional WASM.  BYO-disc model, no assets distributed.","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":13,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-05T10:34:45Z","updated":"2026-10-04T20:06:34Z","license":"Unlicense","branch":"main","homepage":"https://andrewaltimit.github.io/legend-of-legaia-re/","topics":["clean-room","decompilation","game-preservation","ghidra","legaia","legend-of-legaia","playstation","ps1","psx","reverse-engineering","rust","wasm","webassembly","wgpu"],"demo":"https://andrewaltimit.github.io/legend-of-legaia-re/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T21:34:57.862Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T21:34:57.862Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T21:34:57.862Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T22:13:20.213Z","stars":13,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-04T21:34:57.862Z","stars":13,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A playable port and modding hub for the PSX game Legend of Legaia (1998, Sony, NA SCUS-94254), standing on Ghidra-traced reverse engineering of the retail disc. The disc's formats are documented byte-by-byte with provenance back to traced retail functions, Rust parsers extract every asset, and a from-scratch engine runs the game's own scenes, scripts and menus - natively on wgpu, and in your browser via WebAssembly. On top of that sit a disc randomizer, a translation toolchain, and a project site full of interactive viewers that run entirely off your own disc image.","The repo name -re is in both senses: reverse-engineering and re-implementation. This is not a decompilation project: nothing aims at a byte-matching recompile of the executable, and the engine is fresh Rust written from the project's own reverse-engineering record - Ghidra-traced function dumps and live emulator probes - never auto-translated MIPS. Same legal model as ScummVM, OpenRCT2, OpenMW, OpenLara: this repo is code and documentation only - you bring your own disc image, and nothing Sony owns is ever committed or distributed.","Project site: andrewaltimit.github.io/legend-of-legaia-re"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AndrewAltimit/legend-of-legaia-re/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d57d1f4a8868eaf924baa16cbee7079c17608587814a3631492bcd4111531cb4","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T22:13:20.354Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T21:36:05.947Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A playable port and modding hub for the PSX game Legend of Legaia (1998, Sony, NA SCUS-94254), standing on Ghidra-traced reverse engineering of the retail disc. The disc's formats are documented byte-by-byte with provenance back to traced retail functions, Rust parsers extract every asset, and a from-scratch engine runs the game's own scenes, scripts and menus - natively on wgpu, and in your browser via WebAssembly. On top of that sit a disc randomizer, a translation toolchain, and a project site full of interactive viewers that run entirely off your own disc image.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AndrewAltimit/legend-of-legaia-re/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"d57d1f4a8868eaf924baa16cbee7079c17608587814a3631492bcd4111531cb4","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AndrewAltimit/legend-of-legaia-re/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T21:36:05.947Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T20:06:34Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AndrewAltimit/legend-of-legaia-re/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T21:36:05.948Z","hash":"d57d1f4a8868eaf924baa16cbee7079c17608587814a3631492bcd4111531cb4","originalBytes":27844,"storedBytes":27844,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["docs","disc","subsystems","